{# Evidence descriptions shared across review entries. These describe state fields, not additional review requests. #}

{% if kind == 'coordinates' %}
bbox_normalized is [left, top, right, bottom] in page fractions. text_scale_estimate is a rough OCR-pixel glyph-area scale, not actual font size; compare small-print blocks with their neighbours, never classify by this alone.

{% elif kind == 'text_encoding' %}
A raw_text object with literal_parts encodes exact OCR text. Concatenate its parts: strings are literal; {repeat: text, count: N} repeats that exact text N times; {integer_sequence: {start, count, suffix}} emits count successive integers starting at start, each followed by the exact suffix. This is lossless encoding, not a correction or an instruction printed on the page. Repetition alone does not prove a structural error.

{% elif kind == 'asset_text' %}
asset_text_association records a provisional link from an independent OCR text source to a local asset title or caption. The source keeps its own source_order, original text and bbox. This link is an algorithmic hypothesis, not evidence that its ownership or attachment is correct. Audit that source independently. Attached labels do not interrupt the main paragraph's incoming-edge sequence. During page repair, submit the final asset_attachment by stable local asset_id and slot; null detaches it. The initial link is only a suggestion, and repair may create or redirect links. Ignored text and text moved to another ownership/citation stream are never copied back into the original asset. A submitted link must name an actual retained image/table on the current page; it need not have an initial association.

{% endif %}
